  "description": "If your commute is regularly the best part of your workday, then this agile urban bike will have you taking the long way home. Like previous generations of the Shadowlands, the 1 is well equipped and perfectly suited to city riding. A light aluminum frame and plenty of gear options mean that you won't be haunted by the hills on your route. All of that mechanical advantage comes from Shimano’s 10-speed Cues drivetrain. The Cues line provides reliable performance, durability, and easy maintenance – with cross compatibility across the line. There’s no need to leave the bike at home on rainy days, as the hydraulic disc brakes work great in the wet. And if rain is the norm, there are fender mounts to help keep you dry. There are also rear pannier mounts and plenty of bag/bottle mounts, so you can transform your weekday commuter into a weekend tourer.\n\nLower top tube makes mounting and dismounting easier\n\nLightweight 6061 aluminum frame with tapered tubing to add strength\n\nCarbon fibre fork reduces weight and offers a smoother ride\n\nLarge diameter 700c wheels roll efficiently on rough roads and bike paths\n\nShimano MT200 hydraulic disc brakes provide outstanding stopping power in all weather conditions\n\nShimano Cues drivetrain provides smooth, reliable shifting, and the gearing needed for steep climbs and fast roads descents\n\n35mm wide Goodyear Transit Tour tires are fast and grippy on tarmac and bike paths in the dry and the wet\n\nFrame and fork are equipped with eyelets for fenders, racks, bottle cages and bag mounts\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes are designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics are developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
